# Summary of changes for run 6f627fec-f4d2-40ec-ad1c-9e240df5209a
Built the prime-gap ("prime crossword") development under `Catalog/Cryptography/PrimeGaps/`, following the team-loop methodology with Lab Notes (Hypothesis/Experiment/Analysis/Critique/Synthesis) embedded in each Lean file. All main theorems are fully proved (0 `sorry`s, no `axiom`/`native_decide`/`@[implemented_by]`); `#print axioms` reports only `propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound`. Each file is self-contained over Mathlib (verified by full elaboration).

Files:
- `Cryptography/PrimeGaps/Boundary.lean` — defines `nextPrime` (smallest prime > p) and proves:
  • the factorial run `exists_consecutive_composites` / `exists_consecutive_composites_ge` (runs of N consecutive composites, optionally past any bound M);
  • the two boundary facts `gaps_unbounded` and `gaps_unbounded_cofinal` (gaps arbitrarily wide, occurring arbitrarily far out), via the load-bearing lemma `exists_largest_prime_below` + `nextPrime_ge_of_run`;
  • the Bertrand bound `nextPrime_sub_le` (gap above a prime p is ≤ p);
  • conjecture C3: `maximalGap` as a `Finset.sup`, with `maximalGap_le` (G(x) ≤ x), `maximalGap_unbounded` (G → ∞), and `maximalGap_mono`;
  • conjecture C4 (unconditional weakening of Polignac): `polignac_infinite` — for every k, infinitely many primes have gap ≥ 2k (`Set.Infinite`).
- `Cryptography/PrimeGaps/AverageGap.lean` — conjecture C2 machinery:
  • `nextPrime_nth_prime` (the next prime after the k-th prime is the (k+1)-th prime) — the bridge from `nextPrime` to Mathlib's `Nat.nth Nat.Prime`;
  • `sum_gaps_eq` (Cesàro/telescoping identity: the sum of the first n gaps equals p_n − 2, so the mean gap is (p_n−2)/n);
  • `primeCounting_le` (π(x) ≤ x), proved by induction.
- `Cryptography/PrimeGaps/FUTURE_DIRECTIONS.md` — five falsifiable conjectures (sharpened Bertrand p/2 via Nagura; full PNT mean-gap ~ log; Cramér O((log x)^2) for the maximal gap; exact Polignac =2k; safe-prime spacing), each with a "The key insight is…" sentence and a "Why now?" justification, derived from this cycle's results.
- `Cryptography/PrimeGaps/ComputationalEvidence.md` — small-case tables (nextPrime/gaps 2,4,6,8; the L!+2 run; the telescoping identity check), a counterexample hunt up to 1000, and OEIS references (A001223, A005250).

Note on layout: cross-module imports do not resolve in this project configuration, so the files were written to be independent (`import Mathlib` only); the small `nextPrime` interface is therefore restated in each file rather than shared.
